I found no problems in this change. The only implementations of `bookings_on` are the protocol, the in-memory repository and the SQLite repository. All three now have `bookings_for`, so no other implementation of the protocol is left without it.

Both implementations order results by day, start time and table id. Within the SQLite version, `day` and `start` are stored as ISO strings, which sort in the same order as the dates and times themselves. The two repositories should therefore return bookings in the same order.

